  {
   "id": "KQVOZcabCQAJ",
   "from": "mri...@stanford.edu",
   "author": "148ba62e5bd4c791",
   "date": "2018-02-18T08:41:37Z",
   "subject": "Eight schools example using brms",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Paul, <div><br></div><div>I am interested in reproducing the eight schools example with brms. More specifically, I am interested in extracting theta. </div><div><br></div><div>With the Eight Schools Data</div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:13.6px;word-wrap:normal;padding:16px;overflow:auto;line-height:1.45;background-color:rgb(246,248,250);border-radius:3px;word-break:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">schools_dat</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">list</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(227,98,9)\">J</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">=</span> </span><font color=\"#005cc5\">seq(1,8,1)</font><font color=\"#24292e\">, \r\n                    </font><span style=\"color:rgb(227,98,9);box-sizing:border-box\">y</span><font color=\"#24292e\"> </font><span style=\"color:rgb(215,58,73);box-sizing:border-box\">=</span><font color=\"#24292e\"> c(</font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">28</span><font color=\"#24292e\">,  </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">8</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(215,58,73);box-sizing:border-box\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">3</span><font color=\"#24292e\">,  </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">7</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(215,58,73);box-sizing:border-box\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">1</span><font color=\"#24292e\">,  </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">1</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">18</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">12</span><font color=\"#24292e\">),\r\n                    </font><span style=\"color:rgb(227,98,9);box-sizing:border-box\">sigma</span><font color=\"#24292e\"> </font><span style=\"color:rgb(215,58,73);box-sizing:border-box\">=</span><font color=\"#24292e\"> c(</font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">15</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">10</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">16</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">11</span><font color=\"#24292e\">,  </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">9</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">11</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">10</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">18</span><font color=\"#24292e\">))</font></pre></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;d think to run brm(y|se(sigma) ~ 1 + (1|J), data = schools_dat)</div><div>However, I am only able to recover eta and mu. How can I get posteriors of theta from brms output? </div><div><br></div><div> see below for Stan Code from <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/rstan/wiki/RStan-Getting-Started\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/rstan/wiki/RStan-Getting-Started&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451529665000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0fYTtxPnp_7zJTQ-hdqxZ0\">https://github.com/stan-dev/rstan/wiki/RStan-Getting-Started</a></div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:13.6px;word-wrap:normal;padding:16px;overflow:auto;line-height:1.45;background-color:rgb(246,248,250);border-radius:3px;word-break:normal;color:rgb(36,41,46)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(106,115,125)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">//</span> saved as 8schools.stan</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(111,66,193)\">data</span> {\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">int</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&lt;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">lower</span>=<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">0</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&gt;</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">J</span>; <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(106,115,125)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">//</span> number of schools </span>\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">real</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">y</span>[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">J</span>]; <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(106,115,125)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">//</span> estimated treatment effects</span>\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">real</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&lt;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">lower</span>=<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">0</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&gt;</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">sigma</span>[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">J</span>]; <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(106,115,125)\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">//</span> s.e. of effect estimates </span>\r\n}\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(111,66,193)\">parameters</span> {\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">real</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">mu</span>; \r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">real</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&lt;</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">lower</span>=<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">0</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">&gt;</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">tau</span>;\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">real</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">eta</span>[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">J</span>];\r\n}\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(111,66,193)\">transformed parameters</span> {\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">real</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">theta</span>[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">J</span>];\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">for</span> (<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">j</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">in</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">1</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">:</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">J</span>)\r\n    <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">theta</span>[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">j</span>] <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">mu</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">+</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">tau</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">*</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">eta</span>[<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">j</span>];\r\n}\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(111,66,193)\">model</span> {\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">target</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">+=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">normal_lpdf</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">eta</span> | <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">0</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">1</span>);\r\n  <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">target</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(215,58,73)\">+=</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,92,197)\">normal_lpdf</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">y</span> | <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">theta</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">sigma</span>);\r\n}</pre></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
