:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">1</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">18</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">12</span><font color=\"#24292e\">),\r\n                    </font><span style=\"color:rgb(227,98,9);box-sizing:border-box\">sigma</span><font color=\"#24292e\"> </font><span style=\"color:rgb(215,58,73);box-sizing:border-box\">=</span><font color=\"#24292e\"> c(</font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">15</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">10</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">16</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">11</span><font color=\"#24292e\">,  </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">9</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">11</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">10</span><font color=\"#24292e\">, </font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,92,197);box-sizing:border-box\">18</span><font color=\"#24292e\">))</font></pre></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;d think to run brm(y|se(sigma) ~ 1 + (1|J), data = schools_dat)</div><div>However, I am only able to recover eta and mu. How can I get posteriors of theta from brms output? </div><div><br></div><div> see below for Stan Code from <a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/rstan/wiki/RStan-Getting-Started\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/rstan/wiki/RStan-Getting-Started&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451529669000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0zFBBpnXcQzJWY0yJZcijT\">https://github.com/stan-dev/rstan/wiki/RStan-Getting-Started</a></div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"box-sizi